{{ElectionsTN}}
The '''2018 United States House of Representatives elections in Tennessee''' will be held on November 6, 2018, to elect the nine [[United States House of Representatives|U.S. Representatives]] from the state of [[Tennessee]], one from each of the state's nine congressional districts. The elections will coincide with the elections of other federal and state offices, including the [[Tennessee gubernatorial election, 2018|gubernatorial election]].
{{Toclimit|limit=2}}
==District 1==
{{see also|Tennessee's 1st congressional district}}
The 1st district covers the northeastern corner of the states and is anchored by the [[Tri-Cities, Tennessee|Tri-Cities]] area including the cities of [[Greeneville, TN|Greeneville]], [[Johnson City, TN|Johnson City]], and [[Kingsport, TN|Kingsport]]. This is a heavily Republican district with a PVI of R+28. The incumbent is Republican [[Phil Roe (politician)|Phil Roe]], who has represented the district since 2009.  Roe was re-elected with 78% of the vote in 2016.

Roe had initially promised to serve only five terms when first elected in 2008, but announced in February 2018 that he would run again that November.<ref>{{cite news|url=http://www.johnsoncitypress.com/Government/2018/02/08/Roe-to-run-for-re-election|title=Roe to run for re-election|publisher=[[Johnson City Press]]|date=2018-02-08}}</ref>

