==District 2==
{{see also|Tennessee's 2nd congressional district}}
The 2nd district is located in northeastern Tennessee and is centered around [[Knoxville, TN|Knoxville]] and its surrounding suburbs; other cities include [[Jefferson City, TN|Jefferson City]] and [[Tazewell, TN|Tazewell]]. This district has a PVI of R+20. The incumbent is Republican [[Jimmy Duncan (U.S. politician)|John Duncan]], who has represented the district since 1988.  Duncan was re-elected with 76% of the vote in 2016. 
On July 31, 2017, Duncan announced that he would not run for reelection in 2018. He wishes to spend more time with his family.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://hosted.ap.org/dynamic/stories/U/US_CONGRESS_DUNCAN?SITE=AP&SECTION=HOME&TEMPLATE=DEFAULT|title=Associated Press News|website=AP News|accessdate=September 12, 2018}}</ref> His successor will be only the seventh person (not including caretakers) to represent this district since 1909.
