==District 6==
{{see also|Tennessee's 6th congressional district}}
The 6th district is located in middle Tennessee including [[Cookeville, TN|Cookeville]], [[Gallatin, TN|Gallatin]], [[Hendersonville, TN|Hendersonville]], and [[Lebanon, TN|Lebanon]]. This district has a PVI of R+24. The incumbent is Republican [[Diane Black]], who has represented the district since 2011.  Black was re-elected with 71% of the vote in 2016.

Black is running for governor instead of re-election in 2018.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.tennessean.com/story/news/2017/02/09/diane-black-weighing-run-governor-meets-state-gop-leaders/97719424/|title=Diane Black, weighing run for governor, meets with state GOP leaders|work=[[The Tennessean]]|last=Garrison|first=Joey|date=February 9, 2017|accessdate=March 3, 2017}}</ref>

