==District 9==
{{see also|Tennessee's 9th congressional district}}
The 9th district is based around [[Memphis, Tennessee|Memphis]] and its surrounding suburbs including [[Millington, TN|Millington]]. This is a heavily Democratic district with a PVI of D+28. The incumbent is Democrat [[Steve Cohen]], who has represented the district since 2007.  Cohen was re-elected with 79% of the vote in 2016.

Cohen has announced he is running for re-election in 2018 and intends to run in 2020.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.commercialappeal.com/story/news/politics/2016/12/31/cohen-says-hell-seek-reelection-2018-2020/96041090/|title=Cohen says he'll seek reelection in 2018, 2020|work=[[The Commercial Appeal]]|last=Risher|first=Wayne|date=December 31, 2016|accessdate=March 2, 2017}}</ref>

